ok   Cast.binds casts each value the way a relation binds it
ok   Cast.binds feeds Connection#execute
ok   Cast.like_escape escapes backslash, percent and underscore only
ok   Cast.hash and Cast.array narrow parsed JSON, a fresh empty container otherwise
ok   Cast.hash and Cast.array copy: writing to the result leaves the value alone
ok   Cast.empty_hash and Cast.empty_array are fresh on every call
ok   upsert inserts, then updates the conflicting row with the update expressions
ok   upsert binds a Time as its ISO 8601 text and can keep the first or last seen value
ok   upsert with an empty update is DO NOTHING and reports 0 rows on a conflict
ok   upsert writes the table of the model it is called on
ok   upsert refuses empty attributes, no conflict target and names that are not columns
ok   upsert surfaces SQLite's refusal when no unique index matches the conflict target
ok   increment adds to a column over the relation's rows and returns how many changed
ok   increment with a limit or offset changes only that window, by id
ok   increment refuses a name that is not a column
ok   where_like is a substring match with the text's wildcards escaped
ok   where_like quotes the column and binds the pattern
ok   a prefix search writes its own pattern from like_escape
ok   pluck_str, pluck_int and pluck_float read one column in the relation's order
ok   pluck refuses a name that is not a column
ok   count_by counts the rows per value, keys as Strings in order
ok   count_by merges NULL into the empty-String key and groups only the window
ok   count_by_sql groups by an expression: hour buckets
ok   sum_int and sum_float add up a column, 0 for no rows
